            "official_url": "https://www.indiabudget.gov.in/doc/cen/cus1526.pdf",
            "channel": "conditional",
            "applicability_en": "India currency declaration and carriage permits: the Currency Declaration Form (CDF) is a stand-alone statutory form annexed to the Foreign Exchange Management (Export and Import of Currency) Regulations, 2015 (FEMA 6(R)/RB-2015, as amended in 2019 and 2020) and appended to the 2026 Customs Baggage Regulations; it is distinct from the ordinary electronic baggage declarations (CBD-I/CBD-II). A CDF must be filed on arrival only when the aggregate value of foreign exchange brought in as currency notes, bank notes or travellers cheques strictly exceeds USD 10,000 or its equivalent and/or the aggregate value of foreign currency notes strictly exceeds USD 5,000 or its equivalent; at or below both thresholds no CDF is required. Foreign exchange in any form may be brought into India freely and without limit, provided it is declared on the CDF on arrival to the Customs authorities when the thresholds are exceeded; taking foreign exchange out of India is prohibited unless it was obtained from an authorised dealer or money changer or is otherwise covered by general or special permission of the Reserve Bank of India (for example foreign exchange retained under the 2015 Possession and Retention Regulations). Non-residents may take out of India unspent foreign exchange up to the amount they originally brought in and, where required, declared on arrival. Indian rupee notes carry separate capped permissions: a person resident in India may take out of India (other than to Nepal or Bhutan), and bring back on return from a temporary visit (other than from Nepal or Bhutan), Government of India and RBI currency notes up to INR 25,000 per person; a person resident outside India who is not a citizen of Pakistan or Bangladesh may bring into or take out of India such notes up to INR 25,000 per person. Nepal and Bhutan exception: only Government of India and RBI notes of denominations not exceeding INR 100 generally move between India and Nepal or Bhutan, though an individual travelling from India to Nepal or Bhutan may carry Mahatma Gandhi (new) series INR 200 and/or INR 500 notes up to a total limit of INR 25,000, and Nepalese or Bhutanese currency notes may be taken out or brought in. The USD 10,000 and USD 5,000 figures are declaration triggers only, not carriage limits or licences: the authority to carry foreign exchange or rupee notes comes from the FEMA 2015 Regulations and RBI permissions, and any carriage outside those permissions (including rupee notes above INR 25,000, or foreign currency not obtained from an authorised person) requires prior general or special permission of the Reserve Bank. UI supplement (per the manual's published screen flow, not a filing completed in this research): inside the Atithi baggage declaration form, selecting the Currency checkbox makes an inline Currency Declaration section appear within the same CBD form; currency rows are added or deleted with the add/delete icons, the currency type is selected from the drop-down menu, the respective details are filled in, and the total is auto-calculated; the passenger then uses the same 'Save As Draft'/'Submit' buttons as the rest of the baggage declaration. Accordingly, the currency details are captured within the single Atithi baggage-declaration submission; this checkbox-expanded section within the CBD screen flow is not evidence of two independent online submissions.",
            "applicability_zh": "印度货币申报与携带许可:货币申报表(Currency Declaration Form,CDF)是《外汇管理(货币输出入)条例2015》(FEMA 6(R)/RB-2015,经2019年及2020年修订)附件所载、并随2026年海关行李条例一并附上的独立法定表单,区别于普通电子行李申报(CBD-I/CBD-II)。仅在入境时携带的外汇(现钞纸币、银行票据或旅行支票)总额严格超过等值10,000美元,和/或外币现钞总额严格超过等值5,000美元时,才须提交CDF申报;两项均未超过门槛则无需申报。任何形式的外汇均可自由、无限额携入印度,但超过门槛者须于抵达时以CDF向海关申报;携出外汇原则上被禁止,除非该外汇系从授权交易商或货币兑换商取得,或另获印度储备银行(RBI)一般或特别许可(例如依2015年《持有与保留外汇条例》保留的外汇)。非居民携出印度未用外汇，以其原携入并（在需要时）于入境时申报的金额为限。印度卢比现钞另设限额许可:印度居民每人可携不超过25,000卢比的政府及印度储备银行纸币出境(赴尼泊尔、不丹除外),临时出国返回时亦可比照自境外携入(自尼泊尔、不丹入境除外);非巴基斯坦、孟加拉国公民且居住在印度境外的访印人士,每人可携入/携出不超过25,000卢比的上述纸币。尼泊尔与不丹例外:印度与尼泊尔、不丹之间一般仅限面额不超过100卢比的纸币流通,但个人自印度赴尼泊尔或不丹可携带圣雄甘地(新版)系列200卢比及/或500卢比纸币,总额不超过25,000卢比;尼泊尔、不丹货币可双向携带。10,000美元与5,000美元仅是申报触发线,不是携带额度或许可:外汇及卢比现钞的携带权来自FEMA 2015年条例及RBI许可,超出许可范围的携带(含卢比纸币超过25,000卢比,或非经授权人士取得的外币)须事先取得印度储备银行的一般或特别许可。 界面补充（依据手册公布的屏幕流程，并非本次实际提交）：在 Atithi 行李申报表内勾选 Currency 复选框后，会在同一份 CBD 表单内展开显示 Currency Declaration 栏目；通过增删图标添加或删除币种行，从下拉菜单选择货币类型并填写相应明细，总额自动计算，之后与行李申报其余内容共用同一组 Save As Draft/Submit 按钮。因此外币申报内容是在 Atithi 行李申报的一次在线提交中一并采集的；该“在 CBD 表单内勾选展开栏目”的界面流程不能证明存在两次相互独立的在线提交。",
            "timing_en": "Declare currency on arrival; retain the certified CDF for unused-currency departure checks.",
            "timing_zh": "入境时申报货币；保留经签认CDF用于离境携出未用外汇。",
