            "id": "vu-unaccompanied-effects-concession",
            "type": "customs_declaration",
            "name_en": "Declaration of unaccompanied personal and household effects (residence concession)",
            "name_zh": "不随身个人及家庭物品申报（定居优惠）",
            "agency": "Vanuatu Customs and Inland Revenue",
            "official_url": "https://vanuatucustoms.gov.vu/home/section/customs/travellers/unaccompanied-personal.html",
            "channel": "paper",
            "applicability_en": "For returning residents or persons assuming residence in Vanuatu: concessions for unaccompanied personal and household effects are available to those taking up residence in Vanuatu for the first time, and to returning Vanuatu residents after absence of at least 12 months in the previous two-year period. Permitted goods: personal and household effects in the owner's possession and available for use for at least 12 months immediately prior to departure to Vanuatu; one motor vehicle per family changing residence if similarly owned/used for 12 months (right-hand-drive vehicles are prohibited from import); one power or sail boat on a trailer (further conditions on the page). The submission step is proved by the current official form itself: 'DECLARATION OF UNACCOMPANIED PERSONAL EFFECTS' (listed on the Customs Forms page) opens by stating that it is a legally binding document and that the penalties for a false declaration are severe, and instructs that the statement must be completed in Block Letters in English or French; it covers the owner and spouse. Its Yes/No items ask whether the traveller packed the goods and is fully aware of the contents; whether the packages contain goods belonging to any other person; and whether the effects contain restricted drugs, narcotics, steroids or performance-enhancing drugs; restricted weapons, firearms, spring-bladed knives, explosives; products manufactured from endangered species; obscene material; Vanuatu or foreign currency in excess of VT 100,000 - a FORM FIELD about currency inside the consignment only, not a general cash border threshold and not the VT 1,000,000 carried-on-person trigger (see vu-border-currency-declaration); cigarettes, cigars or tobacco; alcoholic liquor; goods for commercial purposes; and other goods owned for less than 12 months - followed by a description/value/date-of-purchase table and the owner's signature and date.",
            "applicability_zh": "适用于返瓦居民或将定居瓦努阿图的人士：首次定居者及在之前两年期间离境至少 12 个月的返瓦居民可享受不随身个人及家庭物品优惠。准许物品：离境赴瓦前已拥有并可供使用至少 12 个月的个人及家庭物品；每个迁居家庭一辆机动车（同样须拥有并使用满 12 个月；右舵车禁止进口）；一艘带拖车、可由客车拖行的动力艇或帆船（其余条件见页面）。提交步骤由现行官方表格本身证明：《不随身个人物品申报表》（DECLARATION OF UNACCOMPANIED PERSONAL EFFECTS，列于海关表单页）开篇即声明其为具有法律约束力的文件、虚假申报处罚严厉，并指示该声明须以英文或法文大写字母（Block Letters）填写；覆盖本人及配偶。其是/否项询问：物品是否由本人收拾并完全知悉内容；包裹是否含本人及家庭以外他人的物品；物品是否含受管制药物、麻醉品、类固醇或兴奋剂；受管制武器、枪械、弹簧刀、爆炸物；濒危物种制品；淫秽物品；超过 100,000 瓦图的瓦努阿图或外币货币——该题仅为表内字段（FORM FIELD），仅就该不随身行李内装载的货币发问，并非一般性边境现金门槛，亦非随身携带的 1,000,000 瓦图触发点（见 vu-border-currency-declaration）；香烟、雪茄或烟草；酒精饮料；商业用途物品；以及其他拥有不足 12 个月的物品——随后为品名/价值/购买日期明细表及物主签名与日期。",
            "timing_en": "Effects must be imported within 6 months of the residency visa being granted (first-time residents) or within 6 months of the last return to Vanuatu (returning residents); the concession can be granted only once. The declaration form records details of arrival (ship/flight, place, estimated time, container number, bill of lading/air waybill, broker/freight forwarder) and is signed and dated by the owner, so the statement accompanies the consignment's clearance.",
            "timing_zh": "首次定居者须在定居签证批出后 6 个月内、返瓦居民须在最后一次返回瓦努阿图后 6 个月内进口该等物品；该优惠仅可批给一次。申报表记录到达明细（船名/航班、地点、预计到达时间、集装箱号、提单/空运提单、报关行/货代）并由物主签名注明日期，故该声明随货物清关一并提交。",
