            "id": "UM-palmyra-private-vessel-approval",
            "type": "travel_authorization",
            "name_en": "Palmyra private-vessel access approval",
            "name_zh": "帕尔米尔环礁私人船舶进入批准",
            "agency": "U.S. Fish & Wildlife Service — Palmyra Atoll National Wildlife Refuge (page directs travellers to contact the refuge manager)",
            "official_url": "https://www.fws.gov/refuge/palmyra-atoll/visit-us",
            "channel": "conditional",
            "applicability_en": "Applies to: a person planning to visit Palmyra Atoll National Wildlife Refuge aboard a privately owned recreational sailboat or motorboat — such a person must ensure that U.S. Fish & Wildlife Service (USFWS) prior approval for the vessel's entry to the atoll has been arranged. The page proves this prior-approval condition on the vessel's entry only: it does not identify who must submit an approval request, does not name the vessel operator as the legal applicant, and names no form or channel — the precise applicant/filing actor and form/channel remain unknown, and no separate individual application by each passenger is stated. Scope: Palmyra Atoll NWR private-vessel route only — not a UM-wide traveller card, and not transferable to any other UM island. Conditions stated on the official visit page: with prior approval, the vessel is permitted access for up to seven (7) days; a maximum of two (2) vessels at one time and no more than six (6) vessels in a single month; documentation of a hull bottom inspection and cleaning showing the absence of any marine organisms, dated within two weeks of departure for the refuge; documentation of an inspection citing no signs of a rodent presence, completed within 48 hours of departure for the atoll; the refuge is open to visitation only when a USFWS manager is present (about six months each year, primarily summer) — contact the refuge manager to discuss open times. The page names no application form, submission medium or fee for this approval.",
            "applicability_zh": "适用对象：计划搭乘私人所有的休闲帆船或机动船到访帕尔米尔环礁国家野生动物保护区的人员——此类人员须确保已为该船舶进入环礁事先安排取得美国鱼类及野生动物管理局（USFWS）的批准。页面仅证明此项针对船舶进入的事先批准条件：页面未载明须由谁提交批准申请、未将船舶经营者列为法定申请人，亦未载明任何表格或渠道——确切的申请人/递交主体及表格/渠道仍属未知，且页面亦未述及每位乘客须另行单独提交申请。范围：仅限帕尔米尔环礁国家野生动物保护区私人船舶路线——并非UM全域旅客卡，亦不适用于任何其他UM岛屿。官方到访页面载明的条件：经事先批准，船舶获准进入，为期最多七（7）天；同一时间最多两（2）艘船，单月最多六（6）艘；须提供船底检查与清洁证明文件（显示无任何海洋生物），日期须在出发前往保护区前两（2）周之内；另须提供未发现鼠类踪迹的检查证明文件，须在出发前往环礁前48小时内完成；保护区仅在USFWS管理人员在场时对到访开放（每年约六（6）个月、主要在夏季）——请联系保护区管理员商谈开放时间。页面未载明此项批准的申请表格、提交媒介及任何费用。",
            "timing_en": "Approval timing: the page proves only that prior USFWS approval must be in place before the vessel's access to the atoll (before arrival) — it does not state that approval must be obtained before departure from any port, and no application lead time is stated. Two distinct document clocks are stated: hull-inspection/cleaning documentation dated within two weeks of departure for the refuge, and rodent-inspection documentation completed within 48 hours of departure. Visit window: up to seven (7) days. Visitation is possible only when a USFWS manager is present — about six months each year, primarily summer; contact the refuge manager (refuge office: 300 Ala Moana Boulevard, Room 5-231, Honolulu) to discuss open times.",
            "timing_zh": "批准时限：页面仅证明USFWS事先批准须在船舶进入环礁（即抵达）之前取得——页面并未述及批准须在任何港口出发前办妥，亦未载明申请提前时限。两项各自独立的文件时限：船底检查与清洁证明文件日期须在出发前往保护区前两（2）周之内；未发现鼠类踪迹的检查证明文件须在出发前48小时内完成。到访窗口：最多七（7）天。仅当USFWS管理人员在场时方可到访——每年约六（6）个月、主要在夏季；请联系保护区管理员（保护区办事处：檀香山Ala Moana大道300号5-231室）商谈开放时间。",
            "fee": "unknown",
