            "id": "PF-cash-declaration",
            "type": "customs_declaration",
            "name_en": "Cross-border cash declaration when entering or leaving French Polynesia (DALIA online, or to customs officers)",
            "name_zh": "出入法属波利尼西亚的跨境现金申报（DALIA线上办理，或向海关关员申报）",
            "agency": "Direction régionale des douanes de Polynésie française (local page); DGDDI (DALIA teleservice)",
            "official_url": "https://www.service-public.pf/douane/reglementations/reglementations-particulieres-et-prohibitions/les-mouvements-transfrontaliers-dargent-liquide/",
            "channel": "conditional",
            "applicability_en": "Direction: both entry and exit of French Polynesia. Travellers carrying cash of an amount equal to or greater than EUR 10,000 — the threshold that is common and explicit across all sources — must declare it to customs; the threshold applies individually to each traveller. The exact XPF equivalent is not unique across sources and is left unresolved: the local customs page (updated 2026-07) and the DGDDI traveller page state XPF 1,193,300, while the COM paper form still offered by DGDDI (2021) states XPF 1,193,317; no exchange rate is assumed and neither figure is adjudicated (see unresolved PF-cash-xpf-equivalent-discrepancy). Cash covers banknotes and coins, bearer negotiable instruments (traveller's cheques, cheques, promissory notes or money orders), highly liquid stores of value (gold) and prepaid cards. Scope: the obligation applies only to cross-border flows, i.e. between the overseas territory and foreign countries (EU member states or third countries) — direct flows with metropolitan France, New Caledonia or Wallis and Futuna are not external flows; however, travellers transiting a foreign territory when departing metropolitan France (e.g. United States, Japan) are subject to it. Carrying cash on behalf of another person must also be declared. Channel is conditional: the DALIA teleservice covers the formality online, available from at earliest 30 days before the travel date and at latest before crossing the border; if not declared online, the fallback is in person to customs officers on arrival. On control, the fully completed declaration must be presentable on paper or an electronic device and the declared amount must exactly match the funds transported; movements of EUR 50,000 or more (XPF 5,966,500 per the 2021 form) require documents justifying the origin of the cash (PF legal basis: article L751-4 of the code monétaire et financier). Cash received or sent by post, express freight or other means of transport falls under a separate customs-initiated disclosure procedure, not this traveller declaration.",
            "applicability_zh": "方向：入境与出境法属波利尼西亚双向。旅客携带等值或超过10,000欧元的现金——该门槛为各来源共同且明确——须向海关申报；门槛按每位旅客分别适用。XPF精确等值并非各来源唯一、留为未决：本地海关页（2026-07更新）与DGDDI旅客页写1,193,300 XPF，DGDDI仍提供的海外领地纸质表（2021年）写1,193,317 XPF；不假设任何汇率、不自行裁决任何一个数（见未决PF-cash-xpf-equivalent-discrepancy）。现金涵盖纸币与硬币、不记名可转让票据（旅行支票、支票、本票或汇票）、高流动性价值储藏物（黄金）及预付卡。范围：该义务仅适用于跨境流动，即海外领地与外国（欧盟成员国或第三国）之间——与法国本土、新喀里多尼亚或瓦利斯和富图纳之间的直达流动不属对外流动；但从法国本土经外国领土过境（如美国、日本）的旅客须办理。替他人携带现金亦须申报。渠道为条件性：DALIA线上服务办理该手续，最早可于旅行日期前30日、最迟于跨越边境前；若未线上申报，后备为抵达时向海关关员当面办理。受检查时须能以纸质或电子设备出示完整填写的申报，且申报金额须与实际携带资金完全一致；50,000欧元及以上（按2021年表格为5,966,500 XPF）的流动须附证明现金来源的文件（法波法律依据：货币与金融法典L751-4条）。以邮政、快递货运或其他运输方式收寄现金适用由海关发起的另一披露程序，非本旅客主动申报。",
            "timing_en": "Conditional channel: DALIA online at earliest 30 days before the travel date and at latest before crossing the border; otherwise the fallback is in person to customs officers on arrival.",
            "timing_zh": "渠道条件性：DALIA线上最早旅行日期前30日、最迟跨越边境前；否则后备为抵达时向海关关员申报。",
